Root cause: npm run dev runs BOTH the worker schedules AND dev-scientific-autopilot
(every 60s) — together they burned 8-9k req/day, over Pro's 7500.

- syncOdds: scheduled runs now use /odds?date=YYYY-MM-DD bulk (1-2 calls per
  date covers ALL fixtures that day) instead of 1 call per fixture (92+);
  manual fixtureIds path unchanged. ODDS_SYNC_DAYS_AHEAD (default 4).
- schedules: ODDS_REPEATED_ENABLED default false (bulk already captures odds
  movement); PREDICTION_SYNC_CRON default once/day (external predictions are
  only 8% of the blend); sync-odds cron */30.
- autopilot: defaults tick 60s->300s, refresh 2h->12h, statistics 1h->6h,
  injuries 1h->4h, plan 15m->30m (all env-overridable).
- scientific-current-refresh weekly instead of every 2 days.
- client.getOdds supports date+timezone params.
- docs/API_CALL_BUDGET.md updated with before/after math (8-9k -> 1.2-1.8k/day).
